{"format":"hologram.registry.artifact/v1","id":"docker.io/envoyproxy/envoy","fetched":"2026-09-25T12:03:15.333Z","source":{"name":"Docker Hub","api":"https://hub.docker.com/v2/repositories/envoyproxy/envoy/","page":"https://hub.docker.com/r/envoyproxy/envoy"},"readme":"# ![Envoy proxy server](https://github.com/envoyproxy/envoy/raw/main/distribution/dockerhub/envoy-icon.png) Envoy proxy server\n\n## Quick reference\n\n- **Maintained by**:\n\n    [The Envoy community](https://github.com/envoyproxy/envoy).\n\n- **Where to get help**:\n\n    [Official documentation](https://www.envoyproxy.io/docs), [the Envoy community Slack](https://envoyproxy.slack.com/).\n\n## Supported tags and respective `Dockerfile` links\n\n\n- [v1.33-latest](https://github.com/envoyproxy/envoy/blob/release/v1.33/ci/Dockerfile-envoy)\n\n- [v1.32-latest](https://github.com/envoyproxy/envoy/blob/release/v1.32/ci/Dockerfile-envoy)\n\n- [v1.31-latest](https://github.com/envoyproxy/envoy/blob/release/v1.31/ci/Dockerfile-envoy)\n\n- [v1.30-latest](https://github.com/envoyproxy/envoy/blob/release/v1.30/ci/Dockerfile-envoy)\n\n- [dev](https://github.com/envoyproxy/envoy/blob/release/main/ci/Dockerfile-envoy)\n\n\n## Quick reference (cont.)\n\n- Where to file issues:\n  https://github.com/envoyproxy/envoy/issues\n\n- Supported architectures:\n\n  `amd64`\n\n  `arm64`\n\n\n## Image variants\n\nFor stable Envoy versions images are created for the version and the latest of that minor version.\n\nFor example, if the latest version in the `1.73.x` series is `1.73.7` then images are created for:\n\n- `envoyproxy/envoy:v1.73.7`\n- `envoyproxy/envoy:v1.73-latest`\n\nA similar strategy is used to create images for each of the versioned variants.\n\n### `envoyproxy/envoy:<version>`\n\nThese images contain just the core Envoy binary built upon an Ubuntu base image.\n\n### `envoyproxy/envoy:contrib-<version>`\n\nThese images contain the Envoy binary built with all contrib extensions.\n\n### `envoyproxy/envoy:distroless-<version>`\n\nThese images contain just the core Envoy binary built upon a [distroless](https://github.com/GoogleContainerTools/distroless)\n(`nonroot`/`nossl`) base image.\n\nThese images are the most efficient and secure way to deploy Envoy in a container.\n\n### `envoyproxy/envoy:tools-<version>`\n\nThese images contain tools that are separate from the proxy binary but are useful in supporting systems\nsuch as CI, configuration generation pipelines, etc\n\n### `envoyproxy/envoy:debug-<version>`/`envoyproxy/envoy:<variant>-debug-<version>`\n\nThese images are built for each of the variants, but with an Envoy binary containing debug symbols.\n\n### `envoyproxy/envoy:dev`/`envoyproxy/envoy:dev-<SHA>`/`envoyproxy/envoy:<variant>-dev`/`envoyproxy/envoy:<variant>-dev-<SHA>`\n\nDevelopment images are created from the `main` branch by Envoy's continuous integration, and are tagged with the `dev` suffix.\n\nImages are created for each of the versioned variants.\n\nFor each variant, images are tagged with just the `dev` suffix and with the `dev-<SHA>` suffix, where the `SHA` is the commit\nin Envoy `main` from which it was created.\n\nFor example, after a build at commit `7c1c4a0e`, an image will be created for `envoyproxy/envoy:dev-7c1c4a0e10a7a0771ac06ce8cf8fa2c6ce86281b`\nand the image `envoyproxy/envoy:dev` will be tagged to it until the next build.\n\n### `envoyproxy/envoy:google-vrp-<version>`\n\nThese images contain tools for testing and researching vulnerabilities as part of the [Google\nVulnerability Reward Program (VRP)](https://www.envoyproxy.io/docs/envoy/latest/intro/arch_overview/security/google_vrp.html)","readmeBase":null,"publisher":{"name":"envoyproxy","url":"https://hub.docker.com/u/envoyproxy","official":false,"verified":false},"registered":"2017-11-07T19:39:37.729265Z","updated":"2026-09-25T04:46:30.581381Z","categories":[],"keywords":[],"license":null,"links":[],"maintainers":[],"stats":{"pulls":5766643536,"stars":181},"mediaTypes":["application/vnd.docker.container.image.v1+json","application/vnd.docker.distribution.manifest.list.v2+json","application/vnd.oci.image.config.v1+json","application/vnd.oci.image.index.v1+json"],"contentTypes":["image"],"storage":23846125587055,"tags":[{"name":"tools-dev-6da46eead1112afa0f4b85b14e3e6ef7d0184761","digest":"sha256:0f575b9512372737ac8c948cfde82363e67e94534a1e6d98f67fe8cbdd4cea23","pushed":"2026-09-25T04:46:30.316249Z","size":194734192,"platforms":["linux/amd64","linux/arm64"],"mediaType":"application/vnd.oci.image.index.v1+json","status":"active"},{"name":"tools-dev","digest":"sha256:0f575b9512372737ac8c948cfde82363e67e94534a1e6d98f67fe8cbdd4cea23","pushed":"2026-09-25T04:46:26.018993Z","size":194734192,"platforms":["linux/amd64","linux/arm64"],"mediaType":"application/vnd.oci.image.index.v1+json","status":"active"},{"name":"google-vrp-dev-6da46eead1112afa0f4b85b14e3e6ef7d0184761","digest":"sha256:b06a0ad6e51165944d95444edd35dc748b9e21f2a86accb8d28b41ae09e78b6e","pushed":"2026-09-25T04:46:10.198946Z","size":176918812,"platforms":["linux/amd64"],"mediaType":"application/vnd.oci.image.index.v1+json","status":"active"},{"name":"google-vrp-dev","digest":"sha256:b06a0ad6e51165944d95444edd35dc748b9e21f2a86accb8d28b41ae09e78b6e","pushed":"2026-09-25T04:46:06.920006Z","size":176918812,"platforms":["linux/amd64"],"mediaType":"application/vnd.oci.image.index.v1+json","status":"active"},{"name":"distroless-dev-6da46eead1112afa0f4b85b14e3e6ef7d0184761","digest":"sha256:7358dc26275a95991746eb1f611323dfb0b65dd5e2f6c75947883485f7e05422","pushed":"2026-09-25T04:45:48.872199Z","size":43708503,"platforms":["linux/amd64","linux/arm64"],"mediaType":"application/vnd.oci.image.index.v1+json","status":"active"},{"name":"distroless-dev","digest":"sha256:7358dc26275a95991746eb1f611323dfb0b65dd5e2f6c75947883485f7e05422","pushed":"2026-09-25T04:45:43.208623Z","size":43708503,"platforms":["linux/amd64","linux/arm64"],"mediaType":"application/vnd.oci.image.index.v1+json","status":"active"},{"na